==Albanian==

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{der|sq|ine-pro|*mendh|t=to pay attention to, be vivacious}}. Compare {{cog|non|munda|t=aim, strive}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌿𐌽𐌳𐍉𐌽|t=look up}}, {{cog|goh|muntar|t=keen, eager}}, {{cog|grc|μανθάνω|t=learn}}, {{cog|lt|mañdras|t=alert, awake, smart, minxish}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|sq|/mʊnd/}}

====Noun====
{{sq-noun|g=m}}

# [[trouble]]
# [[toil]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|sq|mundur}}
* {{l|sq|mundje}}
* {{l|sq|mundim}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|sq|Muji}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|sq|sqj-pro|*māK(e)nT-}}, from {{der|sq|ine-pro|*magʰ-||can, to be able (to do)}}. Cognate to {{cog|lt|mokė́ti||to be able}}, {{cog|got|magan||to be able, have power}}, {{cog|cu|мошти||to be able}}. Alternatively from {{der|sq|ine-pro|*men(s)-dʰ(e)h₂||to learn}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|sq|/mʊnd/}}

====Verb====
{{sq-verb|munda|mundur}}

# I [[can]]
# I [[am]] [[able]]
# I [[beat]], [[win over]]

=====Inflection=====
{{sq-conj-c-a-ur|mund}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|sq|mundem}}
* {{l|sq|mundësi}}
* {{l|sq|mundshëm}}

